New: There are two new functions,
PreconditionChebyshev::vmult_with_last_residual_norm() and
PreconditionChebyshev::step_with_last_residual_norm() that, as a byproduct of
the last iteration step in the respective PreconditionChebyshev::vmult() and
PreconditionChebyshev::step(), also compute the norm of the residual appearing
in that step. While this quantity is not the final residual after completion
of the respective operation, the new option nonetheless gives the
order-of-magnitude of the error remaining after the Chebyshev iteration
without requiring an additional matrix-vector product.
<br>
(Martin Kronbichler, 2026/08/18)
